★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
Cross-checking a sibling metadata entry in the same repo turned out to be more reliable here than a live web fetch would have been: `jdbc-hikari` is a build-time dependency of this very test module (visible in `build.gradle`), so its already-committed URLs are first-party evidence about the parent repo's layout — not a guess. I also grepped every `io.micronaut*` `documentation-url` in the repo to confirm "Maven Central javadoc jar" (not the unversioned GitHub Pages guide) is the dominant, already-accepted convention for libraries without a dedicated versioned guide site — this matters because the task explicitly forbids "latest/current" docs URLs.
